Now, she worked 45 hours total, so the overtime hours would be 45 minus 40, which is 5 hours. Right? Because the first 40 are regular, anything beyond that is overtime. So 5 hours of overtime.

Overtime pay is 1.2 times her regular rate. Her regular rate is $10, so 1.2 times 10 is... let me calculate that. 1.2 multiplied by 10 equals 12. So, her overtime rate is $12 per hour.

