Freda's tomato sauce ended up being 32 ounces after cooking. Since the tomatoes lose half their volume during cooking, the original volume before cooking was $32 \times 2 = 64$ ounces.

Each 16-ounce can contains 3 tomatoes. To find out how many cans are needed for 64 ounces:
$$
\frac{64 \text{ ounces}}{16 \text{ ounces per can}} = 4 \text{ cans}
$$

Each can has 3 tomatoes, so the total number of tomatoes used is:
$$
4 \text{ cans} \times 3 \text{ tomatoes per can} = 12 \text{ tomatoes}
$$

Thus, the number of tomatoes Freda used is $\boxed{12}$.
